// @hash 0dc617a02423
{
  // Off, it files nothing.
  "enabled": true,
  // What the agent may do with its finished work: never push, push only an uncontroversial change, or push once checks pass.
  // Allowed values: "never", "safe", "checks"
  "push": "checks",
  // The model every agent this automation launches runs with.
  "model": "opus",
  // The sources that do not take part.
  "excludedSources": [],
  // Run on a schedule, or when its event fires.
  // Allowed values: "schedule", "event"
  "trigger": "schedule",
  // hour, day (at), days (every N days at), week (weekday at), or cron.
  // Allowed values: "hour", "day", "days", "week", "cron"
  "cadence": "week",
  // Local time, HH:MM.
  "at": "06:00",
  "everyDays": 2,
  // Allowed values: "mon", "tue", "wed", "thu", "fri", "sat", "sun"
  "weekday": "mon",
  // 5-field crontab in UTC (m h dom mon dow), for the cron schedule.
  "cron": "0 6 * * *",
  // An event-triggered run starts this long after the last event of a burst — at most 6× it after the first.
  "settleMinutes": 10,
  // The filed task's description. {{variable}} placeholders are filled per run; {{pushPolicy}} says what the Push setting allows.
  "prompt": "Newer releases are available (seen on main by the Dependency upgrades automation):\n\n{{outdated}}\n\nMove this worktree to them, all in this one task. You own proving it works.\n\n1. Run `./singularity deps upgrade` (in the background — it runs the full check and test suites twice).\n   With no updater named it moves EVERY updater together, behind one baseline and one candidate run: it compares\n   every check, test and the moved inputs' smoke tests on the current releases against the new ones, and writes its\n   verdict to `deps-upgrade.json` in this worktree's data dir (the command prints the path).\n\n2. Verdict `upgraded`: run `./singularity build` and confirm `build-status.json` says `ok`. Then:\n   {{pushPolicy}}\n   A push's message names the moves: `chore(deps): <updater> <name> <from> → <to>, …`. Any authorization to push\n   covers the lock moves and any fix or hold you made for them, nothing else.\n\n3. Verdict `regressed`: every lock was put back. Find the release responsible — one updater at a time\n   (`./singularity deps upgrade <updater>`), then one input at a time within it\n   (`./singularity deps upgrade <updater> --only <name>`). For that release:\n   - If the bug is ours (code relying on old behavior), fix it.\n   - If it is upstream, find or file the upstream issue, then add a hold for that release in that updater's holds\n     file (listed above) with the reason and the issue URL.\n   Then run `./singularity deps upgrade` again over everything, and go back to step 2 on its verdict.\n\n4. Verdict `current`: nothing to do. Everything is already on its latest release.\n\nIf you cannot reach a clear verdict (the command itself fails, a regression you cannot attribute, a flaky gate that\nnever settles), do NOT push: raise a flag describing what you saw."
}
